      "id": "wuthering-heights-s014-p00900",
      "source_en": "Dree, and dreary! I reflected as the good woman descended to receive the doctor: and not exactly of the kind which I should have chosen to amuse me. But never mind! I’ll extract wholesome medicines from Mrs. Dean’s bitter herbs; and firstly, let me beware of the fascination that lurks in Catherine Heathcliff’s brilliant eyes. I should be in a curious taking^(dl) if I surrendered my heart to that young person, and the daughter turned out a second edition of the mother.",
